@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# OpenDisplay Enhanced Next — Mac
+
+Implemented in this source snapshot:
+- Existing OpenDisplay 1.19 virtual-display/touch/pencil support
+- Unicode text injection for Android IME `text` messages
+- Editing/control key injection for `key` messages
+
+The matching Android Enhanced source is required for the new input messages.
+Audio, controller virtualization, Internet rendezvous/NAT traversal, clipboard, and expanded codec negotiation are not implemented in this snapshot.
+
+## Local cursor reclaim
+
+`InputInjector` now installs one listen-only CoreGraphics event tap while a virtual display session exists. It listens only for real `mouseMoved` events. OpenDisplay-generated pointer events carry a private `eventSourceUserData` marker and are ignored. If a physical Mac mouse/trackpad moves while the cursor is on the OpenDisplay virtual display, the cursor is warped to the corresponding normalized position on the main display.
+
+This is event-driven (no polling/timer), so it has effectively zero idle CPU cost. Disable with:
+
+    defaults write sh.peet.opensidecar.mac returnCursorToMainOnLocalInput -bool false
+
+Re-enable with:
+
+    defaults write sh.peet.opensidecar.mac returnCursorToMainOnLocalInput -bool true
